e related contracted read or download operation is called.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-3\",\n  \"given\": \"Legacy spreadsheet or paper-process data exists outside a new configured database and has not been submitted through contracted operations.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-3.3\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The database contains no imported legacy business row and response lists contain no imported legacy records.\",\n  \"when\": \"The API starts and contracted collections are queried.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-3\",\n  \"given\": \"Deployment bootstrap configuration supplies the initial System Administrator identity, warehouse records, and customer-organisation records.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-3.4\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The database contains rows for the configured initial administrator, warehouses, and organisations before contracted operations are served.\",\n  \"when\": \"The API starts against an empty database.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-3\",\n  \"given\": \"A deployment supplies demo seed records and `Seed:Demo` is explicitly enabled or disabled.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-3.5\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The database contains the configured demo seed rows only when `Seed:Demo` is enabled, and contains no demo seed rows when it is disabled.\",\n  \"when\": \"The API starts against an empty database.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-4\",\n  \"given\": \"An active customer account has valid credentials and configured email delivery.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-4.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response contains a challenge identifier, an email message contains the one-time code, and no authenticated customer result is issued before code verification.\",\n  \"when\": \"The customer submits credentials to the contracted sign-in operation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-4\",\n  \"given\": \"A customer challenge is pending.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-4.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"Each response status and returned authentication or challenge value reflects the contract-defined outcome, and only a valid unused code produces an authenticated customer result.\",\n  \"when\": \"The customer verifies a valid code, submits an invalid or reused code, or requests a resend.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-4\",\n  \"given\": \"A customer account requests a password reset.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-4.3\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response values identify token usability, the reset link is sent by email, and a consumed or invalid token cannot reset the password again.\",\n  \"when\": \"The account requests, inspects, and completes a reset using the issued token.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-4\",\n  \"given\": \"The staff identity-provider authorization URL is configured.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-4.4\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the returned value is the configured URL.\",\n  \"when\": \"An unauthenticated client calls the staff authorization-URL operation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-4\",\n  \"given\": \"A customer submits an unknown email address or an incorrect password.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-4.5\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status and error body are the same for both cases, and no challenge value or authenticated result is returned.\",\n  \"when\": \"The customer calls the sign-in operation for each case.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-4\",\n  \"given\": \"A customer submits an expired or previously used code, attempts sign-in for a deactivated account, or calls the staff authorization-URL operation while its URL is unconfigured.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-4.6\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status and error body match a declared failure response, and no authenticated result or unusable authorization URL is returned.\",\n  \"when\": \"The corresponding contracted operation is called.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-4\",\n  \"given\": \"A customer has exceeded the deployment-configured verification or resend attempt limit.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-4.7\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is a declared failure status and no authenticated result or additional one-time-code email message is issued.\",\n  \"when\": \"The customer submits another code verification or resend request.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-5\",\n  \"given\": \"Customer organisations have separate orders, deliveries, certificates, or recall records.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-5.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 403 or the contract-defined not-found status and contains no other-organisation record.\",\n  \"when\": \"An authenticated user from one organisation lists or requests another organisation's records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-5\",\n  \"given\": \"A staff member is assigned to one warehouse and another warehouse has records.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-5.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response list contains only assigned-warehouse records and an inaccessible-record response contains no record value.\",\n  \"when\": \"The staff member lists or requests warehouse-scoped stock, receipts, orders, routes, or quality records outside the assignment.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-5\",\n  \"given\": \"An Auditor is authenticated and a record is available.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-5.3\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The read response contains the record and each prohibited write response status is 403.\",\n  \"when\": \"The Auditor reads the record and attempts a contracted create, update, or delete operation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-5\",\n  \"given\": \"An account has been deactivated or removed.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-5.4\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 401 or 403 and contains no protected record.\",\n  \"when\": \"That account makes a subsequent authenticated request to a protected contracted operation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-5\",\n  \"given\": \"A Quality Manager or Auditor is authenticated and requests a record in a warehouse outside an ordinary staff member's assignment.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-5.5\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is successful and the returned record belongs to the requested warehouse.\",\n  \"when\": \"The account reads that record.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-5\",\n  \"given\": \"A request supplies a valid token issued by the configured Meridian Microsoft identity provider for an active staff account, or supplies an invalid, untrusted, unknown-account, or deactivated-account identity.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-5.6\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status and accessible records reflect the matched persisted account's roles and warehouse assignments, and an invalid or inactive identity receives status 401 or 403 with no protected record.\",\n  \"when\": \"The caller invokes a protected contracted staff operation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-6\",\n  \"given\": \"A System Administrator creates or searches for a product.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-6.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response record contains the submitted product specification and active state, and searches return matching product records.\",\n  \"when\": \"The product is submitted, listed, retrieved, or deactivated through contracted operations.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-6\",\n  \"given\": \"A product has no valid temperature profile or a profile has overlapping or discontinuous tier boundaries.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-6.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 400 and the response error identifies the invalid profile or tier values.\",\n  \"when\": \"The product or profile is submitted.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-6\",\n  \"given\": \"A valid profile change includes an effective date, label, limits, tiers, and reason.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-6.3\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response record and profile list contain the new version, reason, effective date, and actor, while the previous version remains returned unchanged.\",\n  \"when\": \"A System Administrator creates the profile version and later lists versions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-6\",\n  \"given\": \"A product has an earlier profile version.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-6.4\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 409 and the earlier profile record remains unchanged.\",\n  \"when\": \"A caller attempts to alter that earlier version rather than create a new version.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-6\",\n  \"given\": \"A product is deactivated.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-6.5\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 400 or 409 as declared by the operation and the response does not report a successful order.\",\n  \"when\": \"A customer submits an order line for that product.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-7\",\n  \"given\": \"A permitted Warehouse Operator submits a valid receipt with product, lot number, expiry date, quantity, supplier, and location.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-7.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response record contains the submitted values and a Quarantined status.\",\n  \"when\": \"The operator creates the receipt and retrieves it.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-7\",\n  \"given\": \"A product and lot number already have a receipt.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-7.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response contains a distinct receipt identifier and the stock list reports both quantities without merging receipt records.\",\n  \"when\": \"A second permitted receipt with the same product and lot number is submitted.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-7\",\n  \"given\": \"A receipt expiry date is before the current date, or release is attempted when expiry is within 30 days of receipt.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-7.3\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 400 or 409 as defined by the operation and the receipt or release status value is not changed to Released.\",\n  \"when\": \"The receipt or release action is submitted.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-7\",\n  \"given\": \"A valid supplier-format logger file or separate evidence file is available for an existing receipt.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-7.4\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response contains the receipt record or action result and a subsequent receipt response contains the stored file-related record or processed readings.\",\n  \"when\": \"The file is uploaded through its contracted receipt operation and the receipt is subsequently fetched.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-7\",\n  \"given\": \"A handling unit has positive available quantity at a warehouse location.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-7.5\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response record contains the resulting quantity and location, and a movement record contains actor, time, source, destination, and moved quantity.\",\n  \"when\": \"A permitted move or opening-stock operation is submitted.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-7\",\n  \"given\": \"A receipt is quarantined, meets the expiry restrictions, and has no condition requiring a two-person quality decision.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-7.6\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response record contains the Quality Officer as the decision actor and the stock status is Released; this receipt release does not bypass a separately required two-person decision.\",\n  \"when\": \"An authorized Quality Officer releases the receipt through its contracted workflow.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-8\",\n  \"given\": \"A handling unit is allocated to an order and its expiry date ends in the warehouse's configured local time zone.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-8.1\",\n  \"level\": \"job\",\n  \"then\": \"The stock row has Expired status even if it was Quarantined or On Hold, its allocation rows are removed, the order row reflects any replacement allocation, and an audit event and dispatcher alert email call record the change.\",\n  \"when\": \"The scheduled expiry check runs at the start of the next local calendar day.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-8\",\n  \"given\": \"A released handling unit is allocated to an order and has passed its expiry date in the warehouse's configured local time zone.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-8.2\",\n  \"level\": \"job\",\n  \"then\": \"The stock row has Expired status, the allocation count for that unit is zero unless eligible replacement stock is allocated, the affected order status and outstanding quantity reflect the replacement outcome, and a dispatcher alert row identifies the expiry notification.\",\n  \"when\": \"The scheduled expiry check runs.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-8\",\n  \"given\": \"An order contains an allocation that expires and no suitable replacement stock is available.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-8.3\",\n  \"level\": \"job\",\n  \"then\": \"A partial order response shows Partly Allocated status and the outstanding quantity, while a complete-only order row has no allocations and Submitted status; the expired stock row has Expired status and a dispatcher alert row records the outcome.\",\n  \"when\": \"The scheduled expiry check runs.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-9\",\n  \"given\": \"An authenticated customer submits an order with at least one line, positive pack quantities, an organisation-owned address, and an idempotency key.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-9.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"Both response bodies return the same order identifier and the order list contains one order.\",\n  \"when\": \"The order is submitted twice with the same key and payload.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-9\",\n  \"given\": \"A customer submits an invalid line, another organisation's address, a date earlier than permitted, or a product inactive for ordering.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-9.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 400 or 409 and no order row is created.\",\n  \"when\": \"The customer places the order.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-9\",\n  \"given\": \"The serving warehouse has deployment-supplied cut-off, working-day, holiday, and local time-zone configuration.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-9.3\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response record accepts no date earlier than the next working day before cut-off or the working day after that when submitted after cut-off.\",\n  \"when\": \"A customer requests an order delivery date before or after cut-off.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-9\",\n  \"given\": \"An order is not yet Packed or has already reached Packed status.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-9.4\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status and order status value reflect the applicable lifecycle rule, and successful cancellation returns the allocated quantity to available stock.\",\n  \"when\": \"The customer attempts to change or cancel it.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-10\",\n  \"given\": \"Released stock is available for an order from its serving warehouse and has eligible lots.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-10.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response record shows earliest-expiry eligible lots first, applies minimum remaining shelf life, uses greater stability-budget usage first for tied expiry dates, and exposes each allocation and outstanding quantity.\",\n  \"when\": \"The order is allocated.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-10\",\n  \"given\": \"Suitable stock is insufficient for a partial order or any line of a complete-only order.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-10.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The partial order response shows allocated and outstanding quantities without over-allocating stock, while the complete-only order holds no stock until every line can be fully allocated.\",\n  \"when\": \"Allocation is attempted.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-10\",\n  \"given\": \"Multiple orders are submitted concurrently against the same available handling units.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-10.3\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response records and stock list show no unit allocated to more than one order and total allocated quantity does not exceed physical available quantity.\",\n  \"when\": \"The allocations are committed.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-10\",\n  \"given\": \"A dispatcher submits an allocation override with a reason, without a reason, or to stock violating Released status or customer shelf life.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-10.4\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The valid response record includes the reason and changed allocation, while each invalid response status is 400 or 409 and the original allocation remains unchanged.\",\n  \"when\": \"The override operation is called.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-10\",\n  \"given\": \"Suitable stock is released for waiting back orders.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-10.5\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The order response records show oldest-first back-order allocation.\",\n  \"when\": \"The allocation service updates affected orders.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-10\",\n  \"given\": \"An older back order awaits suitable stock or a complete-only order cannot be fully allocated.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-10.6\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response record shows eligible back orders filled in submission order and no stock held by the incomplete complete-only order.\",\n  \"when\": \"Suitable stock is released or allocation is attempted.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-11\",\n  \"given\": \"A Warehouse Operator submits a pack request for allocated stock.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-11.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response record contains the box, logger, lot quantities, operator, and seal time; a reused logger or incompatible packing response status is 409.\",\n  \"when\": \"The requested box contains one logger, products with the same storage band, and a compatible box type.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-11\",\n  \"given\": \"A dispatcher submits a route with date, vehicle, driver, ordered stops, and planned arrival times.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-11.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response record contains the requested route values and a conflicting driver or vehicle assignment returns status 409.\",\n  \"when\": \"The route is created, updated, or confirmed.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-11\",\n  \"given\": \"A route's packed box would exceed qualified duration less the configured safety margin at a planned arrival.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-11.3\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 409 and the response message identifies the box and qualification shortfall or duration overrun.\",\n  \"when\": \"The route confirmation operation is called.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-11\",\n  \"given\": \"A driver calls route listing, route detail, scan, departure, or synchronization operations for the authenticated driver's route.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-11.4\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response list or record contains only that driver's authorized route, ordered stops, expected boxes, scans, and departure state.\",\n  \"when\": \"The driver supplies contracted date, action identifiers, or route data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-11\",\n  \"given\": \"A driver synchronizes queued actions with distinct action identifiers or repeats an action identifier.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-11.5\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response record contains accepted and conflicting actions, and the resulting route history contains each accepted action only once.\",\n  \"when\": \"The synchronization operation is called.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-11\",\n  \"given\": \"A driver submits a handover with receiver, acknowledgement, signature, photo, completion time, and box delivery or refusal quantities.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-11.6\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response record and delivery-evidence response contain persisted evidence and quantities, and refused quantities retain the refusal reason.\",\n  \"when\": \"The handover operation is called and authorized delivery evidence is subsequently fetched.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-11\",\n  \"given\": \"A confirmed route is changed before its driver has left for the affected stop.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-11.7\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response record contains the changed schedule or stop order and an email call or driver-change event is recorded.\",\n  \"when\": \"A dispatcher updates the route schedule or stop order.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-12\",\n  \"given\": \"A contracted receipt logger upload contains repeated, late, out-of-order, future-dated, or pre-sealing readings.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-12.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response record places readings at their occurred times, stores a duplicate once, flags future and pre-sealing readings as excluded from calculations, and shows unavailable-reading gaps.\",\n  \"when\": \"The file is processed and temperature history is requested for its entity and date range.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-12\",\n  \"given\": \"Three consecutive in-band readings follow an out-of-band reading in persisted history.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-12.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response records show the excursion open from the first out-of-band reading until the third consecutive in-band reading and show time charged to each applicable tier.\",\n  \"when\": \"The related temperature history and handling-unit record are requested.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-12\",\n  \"given\": \"A handling unit has excursion history or a late reading changes that history.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-12.3\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response record shows separate budgets for portions with different histories, updated remaining tier allowances, excursion links, holds, and an audit event for the correction.\",\n  \"when\": \"The handling-unit or temperature-history operation is called after recalculation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-12\",\n  \"given\": \"An excursion begins, a tier allowance falls below 25 percent, a tier is exhausted, or a not-permitted range is reached.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-12.4\",\n  \"level\": \"job\",\n  \"then\": \"An email call is recorded within 120 seconds for the required driver when on-route, dispatcher, and warehouse Quality Officers, and affected stock response records have On Hold status pending a decision.\",\n  \"when\": \"The triggering reading is received and processed.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-12\",\n  \"given\": \"A logger has sent no reading for 15 minutes and its box is out for delivery.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-12.5\",\n  \"level\": \"job\",\n  \"then\": \"The response record marks the device silent, shows the gap, and an alert email call is recorded.\",\n  \"when\": \"The silent-device check runs and temperature history is requested.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-12\",\n  \"given\": \"A cold room or its temperature records are available.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-12.6\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response list or record contains the latest reading, status, gaps, alerts, history timestamps, and applicable band and excursion markers.\",\n  \"when\": \"A caller lists cold rooms, retrieves a cold room, or requests temperature history for a room, box, lot, handling unit, or device.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-12\",\n  \"given\": \"A handling unit has recorded temperature history with an interval containing no readings and a stored profile band.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-12.7\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response contains readings in recorded-time order, an explicit gap, and temperature-band and excursion fields for the requested interval.\",\n  \"when\": \"The caller fetches temperature history for the unit or its box, lot, device, or cold room.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-12\",\n  \"given\": \"The configured authenticated logger gateway has a batch of readings for known devices, including duplicate, late, or out-of-order readings.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-12.8\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The persisted reading rows contain each valid reading once at its occurred time, and contracted temperature-history responses show the same ordered readings and calculated history regardless of batch arrival order.\",\n  \"when\": \"The gateway submits the batch through the locked contract operation using its configured credentials.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-12\",\n  \"given\": \"A logger-gateway batch contains readings for a known device, but the request has missing or invalid gateway credentials.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-12.9\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 401 and a subsequent temperature-history response contains no reading from the batch.\",\n  \"when\": \"The gateway submits the batch through the locked contract operation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-12\",\n  \"given\": \"A logger-gateway batch contains at least one valid reading for a known device and also contains a reading for an unknown device or malformed reading data.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-12.10\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 400 and subsequent temperature-history responses contain none of the readings from the rejected batch.\",\n  \"when\": \"The gateway submits the batch through the locked contract operation using valid credentials.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-13\",\n  \"given\": \"A Quality Officer submits a disposition proposal subject to the two-person approval workflow, with disposition, reason, and identity confirmation.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-13.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response record contains the proposal and actor, the proposing officer cannot approve their own proposal, and a different eligible manager's approval or return is recorded without replacing the proposal; this approval restriction does not apply to an ordinary receipt release under AC-7.6.\",\n  \"when\": \"The proposal is retrieved or a decision is submitted by the proposing officer or an eligible different Quality Manager.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-13\",\n  \"given\": \"A quality decision exists for stock that has not been destroyed or delivered, and an authorized caller submits a separately signed superseding decision.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-13.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response record contains the new current decision and the earlier decision remains in the returned decision history; the stock status reflects the superseding disposition, a change away from Released removes remaining allocations and applies the contracted replacement-allocation rules, and a decision that would change the status of destroyed or delivered quantity returns status 409 with the prior decision and stock status unchanged.\",\n  \"when\": \"The supersede operation is called and the decision and affected stock are subsequently retrieved.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-13\",\n  \"given\": \"Rejected stock has a positive quantity to destroy.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-13.3\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response record contains those values and the destroyed quantity is removed from available stock.\",\n  \"when\": \"An authorized caller submits a destruction date, quantity, and witness.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-13\",\n  \"given\": \"A handling unit has tiered budget usage and a related quality case.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-13.4\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response contains the used and remaining value for each tier and linked case telemetry and decision fields.\",\n  \"when\": \"An authorized Quality Officer fetches the unit and quality case.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-14\",\n  \"given\": \"An eligible Quality Manager starts a signed recall for selected product lots.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-14.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response records identify affected stock, warehouse locations, boxes, routes, deliveries, customer response progress, and recalled held stock is unavailable for allocation.\",\n  \"when\": \"The recall is started and its record and trace are requested.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-14\",\n  \"given\": \"A customer submits or updates a recall response for an authorized delivery.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-14.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response record contains on-hand, used, destroyed, and stated-disposition values and recall progress reflects the submitted quantities.\",\n  \"when\": \"The recall response operation is called.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-14\",\n  \"given\": \"A recall has unaccounted quantity or all quantity is accounted for.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-14.3\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 409 for closure with unaccounted quantity and no valid write-off, or the response record contains the signed closure or write-off when preconditions are met.\",\n  \"when\": \"A Quality Manager submits closure or a signed write-off.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-14\",\n  \"given\": \"A started recall has affected warehouse, box, route, and delivery records.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-14.4\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response lists contain the chronological trace of the lot through warehouse, boxes, routes, deliveries, movements, and destruction records.\",\n  \"when\": \"Recall-trace and lot-history operations are called.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-15\",\n  \"given\": \"An authenticated customer requests orders, deliveries, delivery details, certificates, certificate files, or recall notices.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-15.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response list, record, or PDF file contains only records belonging to that customer's organisation.\",\n  \"when\": \"The corresponding customer operation is called.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-15\",\n  \"given\": \"A Customer Administrator submits a valid saved address or invitation, changes an address, or removes an address or team member within their organisation.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-15.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response record or action result identifies the change and subsequent lists contain the updated organisation-scoped address or team record.\",\n  \"when\": \"The contracted customer-administration operation is called.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-15\",\n  \"given\": \"A Customer Administrator attempts to edit or remove an address or member belonging to another organisation.\",\