ent sends the corresponding HTTP requests to every declared operation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-19\",\n  \"given\": \"A caller authenticated as an account with assigned warehouse or organization scopes calls a collection or record operation using contract-defined filters.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-19.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status and returned list or record contain only data within the caller's assigned scope and reflect the supplied filters.\",\n  \"when\": \"The caller sends the HTTP request to that operation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-19\",\n  \"given\": \"The API is running with valid startup configuration.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-19.3\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status for each request is 200.\",\n  \"when\": \"A client requests `GET /`, `GET /openapi/v1.json`, and `GET /swagger`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-20\",\n  \"given\": \"A configured PostgreSQL database and a valid request to a contract operation that creates or changes persistent business data.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-20.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is the operation's contract-declared success status, the returned record identifier and values reflect the requested change, and the persisted row values match that change.\",\n  \"when\": \"A client calls the operation and then reads the affected entity through the corresponding contract operation or directly from the database.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-20\",\n  \"given\": \"A configured PostgreSQL database and a valid receipt input.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-20.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200, the returned record status is Quarantined, and the persisted row status is Quarantined.\",\n  \"when\": \"A client calls `POST /api/warehouse/receipts` and reads the resulting receipt.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-20\",\n  \"given\": \"A customer-owned order that is before packing and a valid order change input.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-20.3\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200, and the returned record and persisted row reflect the change.\",\n  \"when\": \"The authenticated customer sends a valid `PATCH /api/customer/orders/{orderId}` request.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-20\",\n  \"given\": \"An existing PostgreSQL database contains existing records and a reviewed migration introduces the required schema changes.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-20.4\",\n  \"level\": \"job\",\n  \"then\": \"The existing row values remain unchanged and the database table list contains the migrated schema.\",\n  \"when\": \"The deployment migration runs against that database.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-20\",\n  \"given\": \"The configured PostgreSQL database has no tables.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-20.5\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the database table list contains the contract-backed tables.\",\n  \"when\": \"The API starts and a client requests `GET /`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-20\",\n  \"given\": \"The configured PostgreSQL database has at least one table and existing records, and a reviewed migration is pending.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-20.6\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200, existing row values remain unchanged, and the database table list matches its pre-start list.\",\n  \"when\": \"The API starts before the deployment migration runs and a client requests `GET /`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-21\",\n  \"given\": \"A configured PostgreSQL database, valid staff identity-provider settings, and `Seed:Demo` set to true.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-21.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200.\",\n  \"when\": \"The API starts and a client requests `GET /`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-22\",\n  \"given\": \"An empty database with its contract-backed tables created.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-22.1\",\n  \"level\": \"unit\",\n  \"then\": \"The row count in each contract-backed table is between two and five, the rows are based on contract e